# Copy to .env and fill in. See docs/google-sheet-setup.md.
#
# Google Apps Script web app URL that appends demo requests to the sheet.
# Read server-side only — never prefix this with VITE_, which would publish it
# in the browser bundle.
DEMO_WEBHOOK_URL=

# CDN origin for the hero videos, e.g. https://cdn.example.com (no trailing
# slash). When set, ALL clips are fetched from there instead of the app's own
# /assets bundle:
#     hero-desktop.mp4      desktop scrub master
#     hero-mobile.mp4       phone scrub cut
#     hero-desktop-480.mp4  reduced-motion hero + CTA backdrop loop
# Upload each under its plain filename. Leave unset — as local dev and a fresh
# checkout do — and each falls back to its bundled copy.
#
# Worth setting only if the origin serves real HTTP 206 range responses — the
# scrubbed clips seek, and Railway answers a Range request with the whole file
# and a 200, so the browser can't seek and downloads the clip whole. R2 answers
# a real 206. Verify with:  curl -sI -H 'Range: bytes=0-1' <base>/hero-desktop.mp4
#
# Unlike DEMO_WEBHOOK_URL this IS a VITE_ var: it's a public asset URL that has
# to reach the browser, so it is deliberately part of the client bundle.
VITE_MEDIA_BASE=
